-- title:
--   Trace census by ℓ+1 embeddings at level Nℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $N,\ell$ be naturals with $N\neq 0$, let $\ell$ be prime and suppose $\ell\nmid N$. Write $F_M=\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M)$ for the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the series $j(q^{d})$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M$. Assume given units $\zeta,\xi$ of $L$ with $\zeta$ a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, $\xi$ a primitive $N\ell$-th root of unity and $\xi^{N}=\zeta$, together with a proof $hle$ of $F_N\le F_{N\ell}$, and let $E$ denote $F_{N\ell}$ regarded, via $hle$, as an extension of $F_N$. Then there exists a family $\sigma_b$, $b\in\{0,\dots,\ell\}$, of $L$-algebra homomorphisms $E\to L((q))$ such that: every $\sigma_b$ restricted to $F_N$ is $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$; $\sigma_0$ sends the image $\mathrm{heckeBetaBar}\,L\,N\,\ell\,(g)=g(q^{\ell})$ of each $g\in F_N$ to $g(q^{\ell^{2}})$; for $b<\ell$, $\sigma_{b+1}$ sends $g(q^{\ell})$ to the twist $g(\zeta^{b}q)$, i.e. coefficientwise multiplication by $\zeta^{bk}$; and for every $y\in E$ one has $(\mathrm{Tr}_{E/F_N}y)(q^{\ell})=\sum_{b}\sigma_b(y)$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion incarnation of the $\ell+1$ geometric branches of the Hecke correspondence $T_\ell$ in level $N$: the trace from level $N\ell$ to level $N$ is computed, after $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$, as the sum of $\ell+1$ explicit Laurent-series embeddings, and the last two clauses record their effect on the degeneracy images $g(q^{\ell})$. Because the identity holds for every element of the level-$N\ell$ field, and the $\sigma_b$ are ring maps there, it serves as the input to the weight-two Hecke formula on differentials, where it is used by [`ModularCurve.qExpansionDiff_traceDiff_pullbackDiff_smul_D`](thm.html#ModularCurve.qExpansionDiff_traceDiff_pullbackDiff_smul_D).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_traceCensus.lean

